-- B2: the geometric exponent set --
   Local energy on a compact 3D droplet: A^1, A^(2/3), A^(1/3), A^0.
   1/2 is NOT in the set: 1/3 < 1/2 < 2/3, strictly between curvature
   and surface. NO term of a local/geometric expansion carries A^(1/2).
   Consequence: D1-D3 (all local) CANNOT produce the -1/2 dilution,
   consistent with their derived exponents (0, -2/3, 0).

