   N =  128: staggering = 0.04428  vs c/(2 sqrt N) = 0.04419
   N =  512: staggering = 0.02211  vs c/(2 sqrt N) = 0.02210
   EXPONENT: -1/2 EXACTLY, and it is the ONLY enumerated channel that
   produces it. Root-extensivity (E ~ sqrt(N)) is the signature of
   coherent amplitude addition and is NON-LOCAL by the B2 no-go.

